<title>UK: UK film theme park must find fresh site - report.</title>
<headline>UK film theme park must find fresh site - report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Warner Bros and Britain's United News &amp; Media are seeking a new site for a planned 225 million stg film-based theme park, the Express reported on Sunday.</p>
<p>The Express, which is owned by United News, said that the companies had abandoned plans to locate the park in Hillingdon, just outside of London, after problems obtaining planning permission.</p>
<p>It said they were seeking an alternative location in the south-east of England for Movie World, which was to have included a film and television studio complex.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
